      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Grooms Tavern, once a simple grocery store, reopened in 2007 as a historic and cultural center, preserving the town’s early commercial heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://cliftonparkny.gov/about-clifton-park",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Erie Canal opened in 1825, boosting commerce and linking Clifton Park to broader markets across New York State.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clifton_Park%2C_New_York",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Clifton Park preserves over 1,000 acres of rural land, balancing historic roots with modern Tech Valley development and innovative residential design.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://cliftonparkny.gov/about-clifton-park",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Clifton Park’s historic Grooms Tavern, listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2000, reflects the town’s long tradition of preserving significant landmarks.",
